Tia (docs): Opening a quick PR to add a tiny section on parser shims + compact-envelope fallback for tool-calling docs. Need fast reviews on SDK snippets and wording. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1410
Sam (eng-runtime): Please include the runtime behavior: if JSON.parse fails we emit telemetry `parse_shim_applied` and try a compact-envelope coercion. Call out the route-level flags returned to callers.
Maria (sdk): Adding a short JS example, will port to Python after review:
Maria (sdk): ```js
// example
const r = await client.responses.create({model: 'rw-open-7b', input: prompt});
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(r.output_text);
} catch (e) {
  // client helper that mirrors runtime shim
  const parsed = client.responses.parse_shim(r.output_text);
}
```
Jordan (devex): I'll add a minimal streaming-safe variant and a sample prompt that reproduces nested arrays: `Return actions as [[{"name":"x"}]]` so folks can test locally.
Chad (product): Note for customers: Dedicated customers may see extra retry latency when the shim path is used; recommend enabling prefix caching or lowering batch size for latency-sensitive routes.
deploy-bot: Preview deployed for PR #1410: https://deploy-preview.redwood-inference.dev/docs/1410 (checks: lint \u2705, link-checker \u26a0 anchors)
Tia (docs): Plan: update PR with JS/Python snippets, streaming example, telemetry note, product blurb, and fix a couple stale anchors. Target merge tomorrow AM.
